ode.js","Acceso a una comunidad de desarrolladores de IA","Herramientas de visualización de datos avanzadas"],"fr":["Recherche et analyse de données avec l''IA","Développement de modèles d''apprentissage automatique","Intégration avec des technologies comme React et Node.js","Accès à une communauté de développeurs d''IA","Outils de visualisation de données avancés"],"de":["Forschung und Datenanalyse mit KI","Entwicklung von Machine-Learning-Modellen","Integration mit Technologien wie React und Node.js","Zugang zu einer Community von KI-Entwicklern","Erweiterte Datenvisualisierungstools"],"pt":["Ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores","Pesquisa e ciência de dados IPA","Melhoria de projetos com IA","Integração com React, Python e Node.js","CLI para desenvolvedores","Agentes de IA para automação"],"ru":["ИИ инструменты для разработчиков","Исследования и наука о данных IPA","Улучшение проектов с ИИ","Интеграция с React, Python и Node.js","CLI для разработчиков","ИИ агенты для автоматизации"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لمن-developers","أبحاث وعلوم البيانات IPA","تحسين مشاريع مع الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل مع React, Python و Node.js","CLI لمن-developers","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي للآلية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["uv AIエージェント","IPA研究","数据科学","数据分析","研究解决方案","开发者工具","uv AIエージェント安装","uv AIエージェント设置指南","uv AIエージェント替代品"],"ja":["uv AIエージェント","IPA研究","データサイエンス","データ分析","研究ソリューション","開発者ツール","uv AIエージェントのインストール","uv AIエージェントの設定ガイド","uv AIエージェントの代替品"],"ko":["uv AI 에이전트","IPA 연구","데이터 사이언스","데이터 분석","연구 솔루션","개발자 툴","uv AI 에이전트 설치","uv AI 에이전트 설정 가이드","uv AI 에이전트 대체品"],"es":["cómo utilizar uv para la investigación","herramientas de inteligencia artificial para desarrolladores","alternativas a uv","uv vs otros hubs de IA","instalación de uv","guía de configuración de uv","desarrollo de modelos de aprendizaje automático con uv"],"fr":["comment utiliser uv pour la recherche","outils d''intelligence artificielle pour les développeurs","alternatives à uv","uv vs autres hubs d''IA","installation de uv","guide de configuration de uv","développement de modèles d''apprentissage automatique avec uv"],"de":["wie man uv für die Forschung verwendet","KI-Tools für Entwickler","Alternativen zu uv","uv vs andere KI-Hubs","Installation von uv","Konfigurationsanleitung für uv","Entwicklung von Machine-Learning-Modellen mit uv"],"pt":["como usar ferramentas de IA","o que é uv","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores","uv vs outros hubs de pesquisa","instalar uv","guia de configuração do uv","desenvolvimento de projetos com IA","melhoria de projetos com uv"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ инструменты","что такое uv","ИИ инструменты для разработчиков","uv vs другие хабы исследований","установить uv","руководство по настройке uv","разработка проектов с ИИ","улучшение проектов с uv"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هو uv","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لمن-developers","uv مقابل مراكز أبحاث أخرى","تثبيت uv","دليل إعداد uv","تطوير مشاريع مع الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحسين مشاريع مع uv"]}},"owner":"PovertyAction","repo":"ipa-research-data-science-hub","repoPath":"PovertyAction/ipa-research-data-science-hub","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-05T06:20:06.212Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"uv","description":"This skill should be used when working with Python projects that use uv for package and project management. Use this skill for running Python scripts and CLI tools with `uv run`, managing dependencies, creating projects, handling virtual environments, and executing commands within isolated project environments. Essential for projects with pyproject.toml files.","bodyPreview":"# uv - Fast Python Package and Project Manager\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill provides guidance for using **uv**, an extremely fast Python package and project manager written in Rust. uv replaces pip, pip-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv, virtualenv, and more while being 10-100x faster. The skill focuses particularly on `uv run` for executing code within isolated project environments.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- Working in a Python project with a `pyproject.toml` file\n- Running Pytho","body":"# uv - Fast Python Package and Project Manager\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill provides guidance for using **uv**, an extremely fast Python package and project manager written in Rust. uv replaces pip, pip-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv, virtualenv, and more while being 10-100x faster. The skill focuses particularly on `uv run` for executing code within isolated project environments.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- Working in a Python project with a `pyproject.toml` file\n- Running Python scripts or CLI tools that require dependencies\n- Managing project dependencies and virtual environments\n- Executing commands within an isolated project environment\n- Creating new Python projects or initializing scripts\n- Converting from pip, poetry, or other Python tooling to uv\n\n## Core Concept: `uv run`\n\nThe most important command in uv is `uv run`, which executes commands within an isolated project environment.\n\n### Why Use `uv run`\n\n**ALWAYS use `uv run` instead of bare `python` or direct script execution when:**\n\n1. Running Python scripts that depend on project dependencies\n2. Executing Python CLI tools installed in the project\n3. Working within a uv-managed project (has `pyproject.toml`)\n4. Running commands that need access to the project''s virtual environment\n\n**Key behavior:** `uv run` automatically ensures the project environment is current before executing the command. It installs the project into `.venv` and keeps it isolated from the system Python.\n\n### Basic Usage\n\n```bash\n# Run a Python script\nuv run example.py\n\n# Run a Python module\nuv run python -m mymodule\n\n# Run a CLI tool from project dependencies\nuv run pytest\nuv run ruff check\nuv run black .\n\n# Run external commands that need project access\nuv run bash scripts/deploy.sh\n```\n\n### Adding Dependencies Per-Invocation\n\nUse `--with` to include or override dependencies for a single execution without modifying `pyproject.toml`:\n\n```bash\n# Add a dependency temporarily\nuv run --with httpx python -c \"import httpx; print(httpx.__version__)\"\n\n# Specify version constraints\nuv run --with ''httpx==0.26.0'' python script.py\n\n# Multiple dependencies\nuv run --with httpx --with rich python script.py\n```\n\nThis is useful for:\n\n- Testing code with different dependency versions\n- One-off operations requiring special packages\n- Running scripts without permanently adding dependencies\n\n### Running Scripts with Inline Dependencies\n\nPython scripts can declare their own dependencies using inline metadata. This creates isolated environments separate from the project:\n\n```python\n# /// script\n# dependencies = [\n#   \"requests<3\",\n#   \"rich\",\n# ]\n# requires-python = \">=3.12\"\n# ///\n\nimport requests\nimport rich\n\n# Script code here...\n```\n\n**Important:** When a script has inline metadata, `uv run` uses ONLY those dependencies and ignores the project''s dependencies, even when run inside a project directory.\n\nInitialize a script with metadata:\n\n```bash\n# Create script with inline metadata\nuv init --script example.py --python 3.12\n\n# Add dependencies to script\nuv add --script example.py ''requests<3'' ''rich''\n\n# Run the script (uses its own dependencies)\nuv run example.py\n```\n\n## Common Tasks and Workflows\n\n### Creating a New Project\n\n```bash\n# Create a new application project\nuv init my-project\ncd my-project\n\n# Create a library project\nuv init --lib my-library\n\n# Create project in current directory\nuv init\n\n# Specify Python version\nuv init --python 3.12\n```\n\nThis creates:\n\n- `pyproject.toml` - Project configuration and dependencies\n- `.python-version` - Python version specification\n- `README.md` - Basic documentation\n- `src/my_project/` - Source code directory (for apps)\n\n### Managing Dependencies\n\n```bash\n# Add a dependency\nuv add requests\n\n# Add with version constraint\nuv add ''httpx>=0.25,<0.27''\n\n# Add development dependency\nuv add --dev pytest\n\n# Add optional dependency group\nuv add --optional docs sphinx\n\n# Remove a dependency\nuv remove requests\n\n# Update all dependencies\nuv lock --upgrade\n\n# Sync environment to match lockfile\nuv sync\n```\n\n### Virtual Environment Management\n\n```bash\n# uv automatically creates and manages .venv/\n# Most operations don''t require manual venv activation\n\n# To manually create a venv (rarely needed)\nuv venv\n\n# To activate manually (usually unnecessary)\nsource .venv/bin/activate  # Linux/Mac\n.venv\\Scripts\\activate     # Windows\n```\n\n**Best practice:** Use `uv run` instead of manually activating virtual environments. This ensures environment consistency and automatic updates.\n\n### Python Version Management\n\n```bash\n# Install a specific Python version\nuv python install 3.12\n\n# List available Python versions\nuv python list\n\n# Find Python installations\nuv python find\n\n# Pin project to specific Python version\nuv python pin 3.12\n```\n\n### Running Tools Without Installation\n\n```bash\n# Run a tool ephemerally (like pipx)\nuvx ruff check .\nuvx black --check .\n\n# Equivalent to:\nuv tool run ruff check .\n\n# Install tool globally\nuv tool install ruff\n```\n\n### pip-Compatible Commands\n\nuv provides drop-in pip replacements:\n\n```bash\n# Install packages (like pip install)\nuv pip install requests\n\n# Generate requirements.txt (like pip freeze)\nuv pip freeze > requirements.txt\n\n# Install from requirements.txt\nuv pip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# Compile dependencies (like pip-compile)\nuv pip compile pyproject.toml -o requirements.txt\n\n# Show dependency tree\nuv pip tree\n```\n\n## Decision Tree: Which Command to Use\n\n**Need to run code in this project?**\n→ Use `uv run <command>`\n\n**Need to add a package to this project?**\n→ Use `uv add <package>`\n\n**Need to run a tool once without installing?**\n→ Use `uvx <tool>` or `uv tool run <tool>`\n\n**Need to create a new project?**\n→ Use `uv init [project-name]`\n\n**Need to update dependencies to latest versions?**\n→ Use `uv lock --upgrade`\n\n**Need to sync environment after pulling changes?**\n→ Use `uv sync`\n\n**Need to install a specific Python version?**\n→ Use `uv python install <version>`\n\n**Working with legacy pip workflows?**\n→ Use `uv pip` commands as drop-in replacements\n\n## Key Differences from Other Tools\n\n### vs pip\n\n- **10-100x faster** due to Rust implementation\n- Automatic virtual environment management\n- Built-in lockfile support\n- No need for pip-tools or virtualenv\n\n### vs poetry\n\n- Faster dependency resolution\n- Compatible with standard `pyproject.toml`\n- Simpler command structure\n- No separate `poetry.lock` format (uses `uv.lock`)\n\n### vs pipx\n\n- `uvx` provides same functionality\n- Faster execution\n- Better caching and deduplication\n\n### vs pyenv\n\n- `uv python` manages Python versions\n- Integrated with project management\n- Faster installation and switching\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Always use `uv run` in projects** - Don''t manually activate virtual environments; let uv handle environment management automatically.\n\n2. **Commit lockfiles** - Include `uv.lock` in version control for reproducible builds.\n\n3. **Pin Python versions** - Use `uv python pin` to specify project Python requirements.\n\n4. **Use `--with` for experiments** - Test dependencies temporarily without modifying `pyproject.toml`.\n\n5. **Leverage inline metadata for scripts** - Single-file scripts should declare dependencies inline for portability.\n\n6. **Use `uvx` for one-off tools** - Don''t pollute project dependencies with tools you run occasionally.\n\n7. **Let uv manage environments** - Trust `uv sync` to keep environments in sync; avoid manual pip installs in uv projects.\n\n8. **Check `.python-version` files** - Respect project Python version specifications.\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\n# Add pytest as dev dependency\nuv add --dev pytest pytest-cov\n\n# Run tests\nuv run pytest\n\n# Run with coverage\nuv run pytest --cov\n```\n\n### Linting and Formatting\n\n```bash\n# Add dev tools\nuv add --dev ruff black mypy\n\n# Run tools\nuv run ruff check .\nuv run black .\nuv run mypy src/\n```\n\n### Building and Publishing\n\n```bash\n# Build distributions\nuv build\n\n# Publish to PyPI\nuv publish\n\n# Publish to test PyPI\nuv publish --index-url https://test.pypi.org/legacy/\n```\n\n### Working with Scripts\n\n```bash\n# Create standalone script with dependencies\nuv init --script analyze.py\nuv add --script analyze.py pandas numpy\n\n# Run script (uses its inline dependencies)\nuv run analyze.py\n\n# Lock script dependencies for reproducibility\nuv lock --script analyze.py\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Command not found after `uv add`\n\n**Problem:** Added a package with a CLI tool, but command doesn''t work.\n\n**Solution:** Use `uv run <command>` to execute within project environment:\n\n```bash\nuv add ruff\nuv run ruff check .  # Not just \"ruff check .\"\n```\n\n### Environment out of sync\n\n**Problem:** Dependencies changed but environment hasn''t updated.\n\n**Solution:** Run `uv sync` to synchronize:\n\n```bash\nuv sync\n```\n\n### Wrong Python version\n\n**Problem:** Project requires different Python version.\n\n**Solution:** Install and pin correct version:\n\n```bash\nuv python install 3.12\nuv python pin 3.12\n```\n\n### Script ignores project dependencies\n\n**Problem:** Script with inline metadata doesn''t use project packages.\n\n**Solution:** This is intentional. Scripts with inline metadata are isolated. Either:\n\n- Remove inline metadata to use project dependencies\n- Add needed dependencies to script''s inline metadata\n\n## References\n\nFor detailed command options and advanced usage, see [references/cli_reference.md](references/cli_reference.md).\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-05T07:04:22.202Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing ultra-fast package and project management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要超快包和项目管理能力的Python开发代理。","ja":"Python開発エージェントが超高速のパッケージおよびプロジェクト管理機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"초高速 패키지 및 프로젝트 관리 기능이 필요한 Python 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de Python que necesitan capacidades de administración de paquetes y proyectos ultra rápidas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement Python ayant besoin de capacités de gestion de packages et de projets ultra-rapides.","de":"Perfekt für Python-Entwicklungsagenten, die ultra-schnelle Paket- und Projektmanagementfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Python que necessitam de capacidades de gerenciamento de pacotes e projetos ultra-rápidas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки Python, которым необходимы сверхбыстрые возможности управления пакетами и проектами.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يطورون بايثون وهم بحاجة إلى إمكانيات إدارة الحزم والمشاريع فائقة السرعة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage Python projects with lightning speed, replacing pip, pip-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv, and virtualenv, while utilizing `pyproject.toml` files and executing code with `uv run` for isolated environments, leveraging Rust for performance.","zh":"赋予代理管理Python项目的超高速能力，取代pip、pip-tools、pipx、poetry、pyenv和virtualenv，同时利用`pyproject.toml`文件和执行代码`uv run`以实现隔离环境，利用Rust提高性能。","ja":"エージェントがPythonプロジェクトを超高速で管理できるようにし、pip、pip-tools、pipx、poetry、pyenv、virtualenvを置き換え、`pyproject.toml`ファイルと`uv run`によるコード実行を使用して隔離された環境を利用し、パフォーマンスを向上させるためにRustを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 파이썬 프로젝트를超高速으로 관리 할 수있게 하여 pip, pip-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv 및 virtualenv를 대체하고 `pyproject.toml` 파일 및 `uv run`을 통해 코드를 실행하여 분리된 환경을 활용하며 성능을 향상시키기 위해 Rust를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a administrar proyectos de Python con una velocidad relámpago, reemplazando a pip, pip-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv y virtualenv, mientras utiliza archivos `pyproject.toml` y ejecuta código con `uv run` para entornos aislados, aprovechando Rust para el rendimiento.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les projets Python avec une vitesse fulgurante, en remplaçant pip, pip-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv et virtualenv, tout en utilisant des fichiers `pyproject.toml` et en exécutant du code avec `uv run` pour des environnements isolés, en exploitant Rust pour les performances.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Python-Projekte mit Blitzgeschwindigkeit zu verwalten, indem es pip, pip-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv und virtualenv ersetzt, während es `pyproject.toml`-Dateien verwendet und Code mit `uv run` für isolierte Umgebungen ausführt, wobei Rust für die Leistung genutzt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar projetos Python com velocidade extremamente rápida, substituindo pip, pip-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv e virtualenv, ao mesmo tempo em que utiliza arquivos `pyproject.toml` e executa código com `uv run` para ambientes isolados, aproveitando Rust para desempenho.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять проектами Python с молниеносной скоростью, заменяя pip, pip-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv и virtualenv, а также использует файлы `pyproject.toml` и выполняет код с помощью `uv run` для изолированных сред, используя Rust для повышения производительности.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إدارة مشاريع بايثون بسرعة البرق، واستبدال pip و pip-tools و pipx و poetry و pyenv و virtualenv، وفي الوقت نفسه يستخدم ملفات `pyproject.toml` ويعمل رمز مع `uv run` لبيئات معزولة، واستغلال روست لتحسين الأداء."},"useCases":{"en":["Executing code within isolated project environments using `uv run`","Managing Python packages with ultra-fast speed","Replacing legacy package managers like pip and poetry"],"zh":["在隔离的项目环境中使用`uv run`执行代码","以超高速管理Python包","替换传统的包管理器，如pip和poetry"],"ja":["`uv run`を使用して隔離されたプロジェクト環境内でコードを実行する","超高速でPythonパッケージを管理する","伝統的なパッケージマネージャーであるpipやpoetryを置き換える"],"ko":["`uv run`을 사용하여 분리된 프로젝트 환경 내에서 코드를 실행하는 것","초高速으로 Python 패키지를 관리","레거시 패키지 관리자인 pip 및 poetry를 대체"],"es":["Ejecutar código dentro de entornos de proyecto aislados utilizando `uv run`","Administrar paquetes de Python con una velocidad ultra-rápida","Reemplazar administradores de paquetes heredados como pip y poetry"],"fr":["Exécuter du code dans des environnements de projet isolés à l''aide de `uv run`","Gérer des packages Python avec une vitesse ultra-rapide","Remplacer des gestionnaires de packages hérités comme pip et poetry"],"de":["Code innerhalb isolierter Projektumgebungen mit `uv run` ausführen","Python-Pakete mit ultra-schneller Geschwindigkeit verwalten","Veraltete Paket-Manager wie pip und poetry ersetzen"],"pt":["Executando código dentro de ambientes de projeto isolados usando `uv run`","Gerenciando pacotes Python com velocidade ultra-rápida","Substituindo gerenciadores de pacotes legados como pip e poetry"],"ru":["Выполнение кода внутри изолированных сред проекта с помощью `uv run`","Управление пакетами Python с сверхбыстрой скоростью","Замена устаревших менеджеров пакетов, таких как pip и poetry"],"ar":["تشغيل رمز داخل بيئات مشروع معزولة باستخدام `uv run`","إدارة حزم بايثون بسرعة فائقة","استبدال مديري الحزم القديمة مثل pip و poetry"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust installation","Python project with `pyproject.toml` file","Limited to Python ecosystem"],"zh":["需要Rust安装","需要`pyproject.toml`文件的Python项目","仅限Python生态系统"],"ja":["Rustのインストールが必要","`pyproject.toml`ファイルを含むPythonプロジェクトが必要","Pythonエコシステムのみに限定"],"ko":["Rust 설치가 필요"," `pyproject.toml` 파일이 포함된 Python 프로젝트가 필요","Python 생태계에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere instalación de Rust","Proyecto de Python con archivo `pyproject.toml`","Limitado al ecosistema de Python"],"fr":["Nécessite une installation de Rust","Projet Python avec un fichier `pyproject.toml`","Limité à l''écosystème Python"],"de":["Benötigt Rust-Installation","Python-Projekt mit `pyproject.toml`-Datei","Begrenzt auf das Python-Ökosystem"],"pt":["Requer instalação do Rust","Projeto Python com arquivo `pyproject.toml`","Limitado ao ecossistema Python"],"ru":["Требуется установка Rust","Проект Python с файлом `pyproject.toml`","Ограничен экосистемой Python"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت روست","مشروع بايثون مع ملف `pyproject.toml`","محدود بمحيط بايثون"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"6908ac2baf84b73df019e9d0cceeeb124b2bffd0855286fdcb221bae3e30beda","qualityScore":46}');
